## What this session proved and fixed (build `4FC99EB9`, deployed)

**Three root causes found with instrumented proof, all fixed:**

1. **FACE-1 (7-session-old leaked i_lock hang)** — `mxfs_dlm_reload_inode`'s TORN-DISK-SKIP bail returned while holding a raw `down_write(&ip->i_lock)` (and leaked `snap`). The tear is observed cluster-wide, so **all 8 nodes leaked the shared dir's lock in the same round** → the round-12 all-node create wedge. Proven by the message firing on all 8 nodes at the wedge instant + live /proc inspection showing the holder exited. Fixed (kfree + up_write).

2. **Grant-epoch visibility ordering** — `process_remote_grant` woke the acquirer *before* storing `dir_epoch` in the local DLM mirror, so the first dir modify after a cross-node EX handoff saw epoch 0 and every epoch-gated coherence guard was inert → stale-base RMW → durable dirent clobber (run5's `node4_f1.md5` loss, caught in-the-act by P13-COLLIDE at the same byte offset). Fixed: mirror reconciled before signal.

3. **AG↔dir hold-and-wait** — dir-growth allocations (`exact_bno`/`near_bno`) blocked up to 61s on one peer-held AG while holding the shared dir EX → `-110` → dirty-cancel shutdowns. Fixed with a trylock-skip (existing fallback sweeps cover completeness); P36 retry storms dropped 73-85/node → 1-19.

Plus: 4/tcp verified **6/6 PASS** with the inherited FACE-2 reload retry, and the dead P-DBLALLOC detector gate was fixed (it had never covered file-data allocations).

## Result
First-ever clean **8/tcp dir_reuse PASS (8/8, all 24 rounds)** on this run's builds, followed by one FAIL exposing the next root: the **divergent-grow torn map** — test1's in-core dir fork froze at a holey 4-extent map (adopt refused, never re-healed) and its dinode flush published the tear; verify's cold reload then read the torn disk. The enforcement-ready fence exists but is detector-only because naive skip → OOPS; the heal/prevent design is scoped in memory (`sess1-END-state-4FC99EB9-next-divergent-grow-tear`) with the exact diagnosis steps for the next session.

(To the user's note: thanks for the test1-32 offer — all 32 share the single LIO/tcm_loop LUN, so true parallel clusters need a second backing file + coord-namespace separation; I noted it as an option if wall-clock becomes the bottleneck.)

**Next session picks up**: diagnose why test1's map went holey (run7 dumps saved in scratchpad), fix the heal path, then drive 8/tcp to consecutive clean runs → 4/2/1 regression → full `./run.sh N tcp` suites → marker.

